"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/495","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/495/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/495/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/495/events","html_url":"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/495","id":1613972282,"node_id":"I_kwDOALhqyM5gM0M6","number":495,"title":"Color Output on github actions","user":{"login":"ecs-jnguyen","id":78230502,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MjMwNTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78230502?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ecs-jnguyen","html_url":"https://github.com/ecs-jnguyen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ecs-jnguyen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ecs-jnguyen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ecs-jnguyen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ecs-jnguyen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ecs-jnguyen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ecs-jnguyen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ecs-jnguyen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ecs-jnguyen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ecs-jnguyen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2023-03-07T18:16:55Z","updated_at":"2023-04-06T08:08:08Z","closed_at":"2023-04-06T08:08:08Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hello, I am trying to use structlog in a github action job and I noticed that there isn't any color output. Is there a setting that I'm missing to enable colors in github actions?\r\n\r\nHere's my github actions job run:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/ecs-jnguyen/test-actions-colors/actions/runs/4357219988/jobs/7616263866\r\n\r\nHere is the python code that I'm using:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport structlog\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    logger = structlog.get_logger()\r\n    logger.info(\"hello\", name=\"me\", age=123)\r\n    logger.warning(\"bye\", name=\"me\", age=123)\r\n    logger.error(\"ohno\", name=\"me\", age=123)\r\n```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/495/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/495/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/390","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/390/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/390/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/390/events","html_url":"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/390","id":1092126730,"node_id":"I_kwDOALhqyM5BGIgK","number":390,"title":"Narrow return types of `BindableLogger.{bind,unbind,try_unbind,new}` in `FilteringBoundLogger`","user":{"login":"aucampia","id":4481387,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODEzODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4481387?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aucampia","html_url":"https://github.com/aucampia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aucampia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aucampia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aucampia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aucampia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aucampia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aucampia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aucampia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aucampia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aucampia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2022-01-02T23:38:44Z","updated_at":"2022-01-12T08:47:19Z","closed_at":"2022-01-12T08:47:19Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I usually use structlog like this:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport structlog\r\nfrom structlog.types import FilteringBoundLogger\r\n\r\nlogger: FilteringBoundLogger = structlog.get_logger(__name__)\r\n\r\nlog = cast(FilteringBoundLogger, logger.bind(something=\"value\")\r\nlog.info(\"event description\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt would be nice to not have to cast the result of bind, one option for this would be to just override `{bind,unbind,try_unbind,new}` in `FilteringBoundLogger` to return `FilteringBoundLogger`.\r\n\r\nI would be happy to make a PR for this, but this is somewhat of a commitment that I think would be best to discuss before a change is made, so please let me know if you are open to this. I started some work on it [here](https://github.com/hynek/structlog/compare/main...aucampia:iwana-20220103T0035-narrow_return_type), to show the concept.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/390/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/390/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/165","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/165/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/165/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/165/events","html_url":"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/165","id":330151163,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMzAxNTExNjM=","number":165,"title":"Permission to generate stubs for structlog in typeshed","user":{"login":"waseem18","id":5843007,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NDMwMDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5843007?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/waseem18","html_url":"https://github.com/waseem18","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/waseem18/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/waseem18/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/waseem18/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/waseem18/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/waseem18/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/waseem18/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/waseem18/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/waseem18/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/waseem18/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":14,"created_at":"2018-06-07T07:34:09Z","updated_at":"2021-04-09T18:35:08Z","closed_at":"2021-04-09T18:35:08Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi Hynek,\r\n\r\nI would like to add stubs for structlog to https://github.com/python/typeshed, a repository used to store PEP 484 type signatures for the Python stdlib and popular third party libraries. As per PEP 484, permission is required from the library owner before merging type signatures into typeshed - https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0484/#the-typeshed-repo\r\n\r\nThese stubs will be used by mypy and Pycharm. I'll start working on creating stubs after I get permission from you and do let me know if you have any suggestions.\r\n\r\nThanks","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/165/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/165/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/294","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/294/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/294/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/294/events","html_url":"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/294","id":781773927,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU3ODE3NzM5Mjc=","number":294,"title":"Type annotation compatibility for context_class","user":{"login":"kkozmic","id":117943,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk0Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/117943?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kkozmic","html_url":"https://github.com/kkozmic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kkozmic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kkozmic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kkozmic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kkozmic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kkozmic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kkozmic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kkozmic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kkozmic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kkozmic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":51899758,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1MTg5OTc1OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/labels/duplicate","name":"duplicate","color":"cccccc","default":true,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2021-01-08T01:31:18Z","updated_at":"2021-02-18T06:05:49Z","closed_at":"2021-01-08T08:26:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I'm just in the process or upgrading to version `20.2.0` and I've got mypy complaining about the following\r\n\r\n```python\r\n    context_class = structlog.threadlocal.wrap_dict(dict)\r\n\r\n    structlog.configure(\r\n        context_class=context_class,\r\n        ...,\r\n    )\r\n```\r\n\r\n`structlog.threadlocal.wrap_dict` return type is annotated as `Type[MutableMapping[str, Any]]`\r\n`context_class` parameter of `structlog.configure()` is annotated as `Optional[Type[Union[Dict[str, Any], Dict[Any, Any]]]]`\r\n\r\nSo I'm getting `MutableMapping[str, Any]` where `Dict[str, Any]` is expected.\r\nThe code works just fine (it's pretty much the same as [this example from the documentation](https://www.structlog.org/en/stable/api.html#structlog.threadlocal.tmp_bind)) so I'm guessing the issue really is just overzealous type annotation?\r\n\r\nOr is what I'm doing no longer valid/recommended (and if so what's the alternative)?","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/294/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/290","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/290/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/290/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/290/events","html_url":"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/290","id":777249890,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU3NzcyNDk4OTA=","number":290,"title":"New release (20.2) has a typing issue","user":{"login":"sobolevn","id":4660275,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjAyNzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4660275?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sobolevn","html_url":"https://github.com/sobolevn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sobolevn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sobolevn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sobolevn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sobolevn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sobolevn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sobolevn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sobolevn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sobolevn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sobolevn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2021-01-01T09:19:25Z","updated_at":"2021-01-08T08:29:52Z","closed_at":"2021-01-05T07:12:04Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"My CI fails for a new `structlog` release: https://github.com/wemake-services/wemake-django-template/pull/1418/checks?check_run_id=1632259635#step:7:861\r\n\r\nHere's what happens:\r\n\r\n```\r\nmypy manage.py server tests/test_apps/test_main/test_models/test_migrations/test_blog_post_migrations.py tests/test_apps/test_main/test_models/test_blog_post_model.py tests/test_apps/test_main/test_views/test_index_view.py tests/conftest.py tests/test_server/test_urls.py\r\nserver/settings/components/logging.py:73: error: Argument \"context_class\" to \"configure\" has incompatible type \"Type[MutableMapping[str, Any]]\"; expected \"Union[Type[Dict[str, Any]], Type[Dict[Any, Any]], None]\"\r\nFound 1 error in 1 file (checked 28 source files)\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere's the source code which works correctly with `20.1`: https://github.com/wemake-services/wemake-django-template/blob/master/%7B%7Bcookiecutter.project_name%7D%7D/server/settings/components/logging.py#L73\r\n\r\nP.S. Happy New Year! 🎄 ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/290/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/290/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}